/*
postCreateCommand
-----------------

The third and final setup hook (`initCommand`, `updateContentCommand`,
`postCreateCommand`).

• Runs **inside** the container **after** `updateContentCommand`, once the
  container is assigned to a user for the first time.
• At this stage, you can access user-scoped secrets and permissions—cloud
  providers execute this hook only after the container becomes user-specific.
• If you supply an array, it is run directly (no shell wrapper).

---

**Viewing the output**

In the JetBrains client IDE, choose **Help ▸ Collect Host and Client Logs**.
Unzip the archive and open `Host/idea.log` to see the command’s terminal
output.
*/
{
  "name": "spec-lifecycle_postCreateCommand",
  "image": "ubuntu:latest",
  //  "postCreateCommand": "echo 'Initializing Dev Container...'"
  //  "postCreateCommand": ["sh", "-c", "echo 'Initializing Dev Container...'"]
  "postCreateCommand": {
    "1": "ls /",
    "2": "echo 'PostCreateCommand...'",
    "3": "echo 'ok'"
  }
}
